  "path": "ordinary-source",
  "scope": "Two independent author roots reproduce the complete WIT archive. Author and build roots are removed before offline installation. One independently compiled public C caller executes the actual Component Model host before and after moving the installed tree, for two executions per selection. Caller source and compilation tools are removed before execution. Generated package sources remain installed. The full fixture checks per-use constructor selection and normalization, repeated record fields, active variant branches, aliases, mixed Fin guards, exact rejection paths, caller-input preservation and recovery. Nominal acceptance covers the tested Nat Subtype records, variants, aliases, nested copied containers and constructor-free results on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor, Wasmtime 42.0.1 and wasm-tools 1.245.1. Two independent author builds reproduce each archive. Author/build roots are removed before offline installation, and caller compilation inputs are removed before the identical executable runs and replays after relocation. Generated package sources remain installed. The Component Model adapter requires its native host and is not a standalone WASI command. Other primitive-base nominal fixtures, refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured; local runs do not establish hosted 2.38 release-floor acceptance. The archive retains original text members, compiled components and caller binaries, but not complete native archives or native libraries. Compiler and operating system distributions remain trusted. The launcher did not record its own pre-launch digest, Node executable path or full ambient environment; the command reconstructs its captured arguments and recorded tool/selection values. Two independent author roots reproduce the complete WIT archive. Author and build roots are removed before offline installation. One independently compiled public C caller executes the actual Component Model host before and after moving the installed tree, for two executions per selection. Caller source and compilation tools are removed before execution. Generated package sources remain installed. The standalone result-only fixture projects scalars, structural containers, records, variants and aliases without input constructor choices, including 100-bit Nat results. Nominal acceptance covers the tested Nat Subtype records, variants, aliases, nested copied containers and constructor-free results on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor, Wasmtime 42.0.1 and wasm-tools 1.245.1. Two independent author builds reproduce each archive. Author/build roots are removed before offline installation, and caller compilation inputs are removed before the identical executable runs and replays after relocation. Generated package sources remain installed. The Component Model adapter requires its native host and is not a standalone WASI command. Other primitive-base nominal fixtures, refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured; local runs do not establish hosted 2.38 release-floor acceptance. The archive retains original text members, compiled components and caller binaries, but not complete native archives or native libraries. Compiler and operating system distributions remain trusted. The launcher did not record its own pre-launch digest, Node executable path or full ambient environment; the command reconstructs its captured arguments and recorded tool/selection values.",
  "hostTypes": {
